  "source_parent": "b6bf37b91da906146f2ccf5da59bf5d391f3502d",
  "scope": "Derive radix alignment positivity from exponential monotonicity and positive products",
  "validation": "Paired target and both tracked direct Lean clients pass with byte-identical client objects. Three-object-pinned probes show eight matching target declaration/type/axiom reports and matching default simp and instance censuses. Source-current CarrierSoundness and PellPowerRecovery direct provider pairs match prior producer receipts.",
  "limitations": [
    "Historical CarrierSoundness and PowerRecovery producer builds pinned FirstIndex whose producer pinned pre-477b3197a1 FirstNorm. These are historical producer pins, not independent measurements of transitive objects loaded by the present builds.",
    "Further construction clients and the wider project, Foundation and Mathlib transitive closure were not rebuilt. Direct source/object producer associations do not establish a fully current-source closure.",
    "Census comparisons cover declarations, types, axioms and stated registrations, not proof bodies or every persistent environment extension. One shared-load CPU timing pair is not a general benchmark. Author records predate the commit; the independent review/audit verify commit and parent sources.",
    "Compiled objects and cached overlays are omitted. Recorded paths include temporary /dev/shm objects and require those external objects for independent byte verification."
  ],
